<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasan Buzurg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1356</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Hasan the Tall, Taj al-Din Hasan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasan Buzurg ('Hasan the Tall') was a Mongol emir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalairs">Jalayir tribe</a> and founder of the Jalayirid dynasty. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> Abu Sa'id died in 1335, he raised puppet khans and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chupanids">Chupanids</a> for control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>'s heartlands, securing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> by 1340. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaykh-uways">Shaykh Uways</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasan-buzurg.jpg" alt="Hasan Buzurg" width="320" height="168" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 14th century · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jalayrids._temp._Shaykh_Hasan_Buzurg._AH_736-757_AD_1335-1356._Baghdad_mint._Dated_AH_749%3F_(AD_1348-9)._Reverse_legend_al-sultan_al-a%E2%80%98zam_khan_khallada_mulkahu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
